## Report: `det-section-heading.md` (PDCA handbook page)

### What was written

A full **PDCA** handbook page for **`DET.SECTION.HEADING`** was authored from:

- `docs/design/ux-audit/deterministic-design-rules.md` (each major section → one heading; outline order)
- `design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-section-heading.check.js` (45-word / 48px thresholds, three violation kinds, exclusions)
- KS patterns: `doc-main`, `forge-section`, `ks-section`, `section-label`, `font-display`, `forge-support`, `handbook_page` header band

**Sections included:** Purpose (Plan/Do/Check/Adjust), Passing signals, Failing signals, Before/After HTML, Evidence and remediation, Related rules.

**Violation kinds documented:**

| Kind | Severity | Trigger |
|------|----------|---------|
| `missing-section-heading` | minor | Major `section`/`article` (≥45 words) with no `h2`–`h6` (eyebrow `p.section-label` alone fails) |
| `duplicate-section-heading` | major | More than one primary heading in the same major section |
| `skipped-heading-level` | major | Outline jumps ranks (e.g. `h2` → `h4`) |

**Before/After examples** use real KS classes (`doc-main`, `forge-section`, `ks-section`, `section-label`, `text-cyan`, `font-display`, `forge-support`, `forge-border`) and demonstrate both missing-section-heading and skipped-level failures vs. corrected `h2`/`h3` ladder.

**Related rules in front matter:** `DET.SECTION.SINGLE_JOB`, `DET.PROSE.LENGTH`, `DET.LANDMARKS.REQUIRED`, `DET.LAYOUT.GRID_CONSISTENCY`, `DET.NAV.IN_PAGE_TOC`, `DET.PY.OPTIONAL_REGIONS`, `DET.HTML.EMPTY_INLINE`, `AI.NARRATIVE.COHERENCE`, `AI.CONTEXT.COGNITIVE_CLARITY`, `AI.VISUAL.HIERARCHY`.

